<article class="env-example" id="0EWI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EWI">Example <span data-tag="0EWI">7.14.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Cov}(\mathcal{C}) \supset \text{Cov}'(\mathcal{C})  \]
</div>
  <p> be two sets of families of morphisms with fixed target which turn $\mathcal{C}$ into a site. Denote $\mathcal{C}_\tau $ the site corresponding to $\text{Cov}(\mathcal{C})$ and $\mathcal{C}_{\tau '}$ the site corresponding to $\text{Cov}'(\mathcal{C})$. We claim the identity functor on $\mathcal{C}$ defines a morphism of sites </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \epsilon : \mathcal{C}_\tau \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}_{\tau '}  \]
</div>
  <p> Namely, observe that $\text{id} : \mathcal{C}_{\tau '} \to \mathcal{C}_\tau $ is continuous as every $\tau '$-covering is a $\tau $-covering. Thus the functor $\epsilon _* = \text{id}^ s$ is the identity functor on underlying presheaves. Hence the left adjoint $\epsilon ^{-1}$ of $\epsilon _*$ sends a $\tau '$-sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ to the $\tau $-sheafification of $\mathcal{F}$ (by the universal property of sheafification). Finite limits of $\tau '$-sheaves agree with finite limits of presheaves (Lemma <a href="/tag/00W2" data-tag="00W2">7.10.1</a>) and $\tau $-sheafification commutes with finite limits (Lemma <a href="/tag/00WJ" data-tag="00WJ">7.10.15</a>). Thus $\epsilon ^{-1}$ is left exact. Since $\epsilon ^{-1}$ is a left adjoint it is also right exact (Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0039" data-tag="0039">4.24.6</a>). Thus $\epsilon ^{-1}$ is exact and we have checked all the conditions of Definition <a href="/tag/00X1" data-tag="00X1">7.14.1</a>. </p>
</article>